    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the volume of the right rectangular prism, we need to determine the lengths of its three sides, which we will call \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). We are given the areas of three of its faces: \\(ab = 24 \\, \\text{cm}^2\\), \\(bc = 32 \\, \\text{cm}^2\\), and \\(ca = 48 \\, \\text{cm}^2\\).\n\nFirst, we multiply all three equations together:\n\\[\n(ab)(bc)(ca) = 24 \\cdot 32 \\cdot 48\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\na^2 b^2 c^2 = 24 \\cdot 32 \\cdot 48\n\\]\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get:\n\\[\nabc = \\sqrt{24 \\cdot 32 \\cdot 48}\n\\]\nWe can simplify the expression under the square root by factoring:\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\cdot 3, \\quad 32 = 2^5, \\quad 48 = 2^4 \\cdot 3\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n24 \\cdot 32 \\cdot 48 = (2^3 \\cdot 3) \\cdot (2^5) \\cdot (2^4 \\cdot 3) = 2^{3+5+4} \\cdot 3^{1+1} = 2^{12} \\cdot 3^2\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\nabc = \\sqrt{2^{12} \\cdot 3^2} = 2^6 \\cdot 3 = 64 \\cdot 3 = 192\n\\]\nTherefore, the volume of the prism is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{192}\n\\]",
