    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the volume of the right, rectangular prism, we need to determine the dimensions of its base and height. Let's denote the dimensions of the base as \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), and the height as \\(h\\). The areas of the three faces are given as follows:\n\n1. The area of the face with dimensions \\(a\\) and \\(h\\) is \\(ah = 24 \\hspace{.6mm} \\mathrm{cm}^2\\).\n2. The area of the face with dimensions \\(b\\) and \\(h\\) is \\(bh = 32 \\hspace{.6mm} \\mathrm{cm}^2\\).\n3. The area of the face with dimensions \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is \\(ab = 48 \\hspace{.6mm} \\mathrm{cm}^2\\).\n\nWe need to find the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(h\\) that satisfy these equations. First, we can express \\(h\\) in terms of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) from the first equation:\n\n\\[ h = \\frac{24}{a} \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(h\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[ b \\left( \\frac{24}{a} \\right) = 32 \\implies b = \\frac{32a}{24} = \\frac{4a}{3} \\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\(b\\) into the third equation:\n\n\\[ a \\left( \\frac{4a}{3} \\right) = 48 \\implies \\frac{4a^2}{3} = 48 \\implies 4a^2 = 144 \\implies a^2 = 36 \\implies a = 6 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 6\\), we can find \\(b\\) and \\(h\\):\n\n\\[ b = \\frac{4a}{3} = \\frac{4 \\cdot 6}{3} = 8 \\]\n\\[ h = \\frac{24}{a} = \\frac{24}{6} = 4 \\]\n\nThe volume \\(V\\) of the prism is given by the product of its base area and height:\n\n\\[ V = a \\cdot b \\cdot h = 6 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 4 = 192 \\hspace{.6mm} \\mathrm{cm}^3 \\]\n\nThus, the volume of the prism is \\(\\boxed{192}\\).",
