    "text": "To find the volume of the right rectangular prism, we need to determine the dimensions of the prism. Let's denote the dimensions of the prism as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). The areas of the three faces are given as \\(ab = 24 \\hspace{.6mm} \\mathrm{cm}^2\\), \\(bc = 32 \\hspace{.6mm} \\mathrm{cm}^2\\), and \\(ca = 48 \\hspace{.6mm} \\mathrm{cm}^2\\).\n\nFirst, we multiply all three equations together:\n\\[\n(ab)(bc)(ca) = 24 \\times 32 \\times 48\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\na^2 b^2 c^2 = 24 \\times 32 \\times 48\n\\]\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get:\n\\[\nabc = \\sqrt{24 \\times 32 \\times 48}\n\\]\nNext, we calculate the product inside the square root:\n\\[\n24 \\times 32 = 768\n\\]\n\\[\n768 \\times 48 = 36864\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\nabc = \\sqrt{36864} = 192\n\\]\nTherefore, the volume of the prism is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{192}\n\\]",
